.Dd November 16, 2026
.Dt USERADD 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm useradd
.Nd create a user account
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl m
.Op Fl d Ar home
.Op Fl s Ar shell
.Op Fl u Ar uid
.Op Fl g Ar group
.Op Fl G Ar list
.Op Fl c Ar gecos
.Ar name
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
adds a record to
.Pa /etc/passwd ,
creates or reuses the primary group in
.Pa /etc/group ,
and creates a locked record in
.Pa /etc/shadow .
Without
.Fl u
the next regular uid at or above 1000 is allocated monotonically.
Without
.Fl g
a same-name primary group with the same numeric id is created.
.Pp
The
.Fl m
option creates the home directory with mode 0700 and copies the regular files from
.Pa /etc/skel .
The
.Fl G
option takes a comma-separated list of existing supplementary groups; at most 16 are
accepted.
.Pp
The 0.2.0 tools are root-only.
Home ownership and non-root execution arrive with the kernel
credential work in U3.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/shadow -compact
.It Pa /etc/passwd
account records, mode 0644
.It Pa /etc/group
group records, mode 0644
.It Pa /etc/shadow
password records, mode 0600
.It Pa /etc/.pwd.lock
exclusive update lock
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A usage error exits with status 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr adduser 1 ,
.Xr groupadd 1 ,
.Xr passwd 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD.
